This strategy aim to remove obstacles that prevent maintenance and reuse through the use of an index in the form of a label showing how repairable a product is. The index will be based on five criteria:

1. The documentation provided by the manufacturer;
1. The ease with which the product can be disassembled;
1. The availability of spare parts;
1. The relationship between the price of the most expensive spare part and the price of the whole product;
1. A fifth criterion specific to the category of the product in question (in the case of smartphones, for example, software updates will be evaluated);

Based on the criteria, the product will receive a score.
